cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this knowledge graph or its data in research, teaching, or products, please cite it as below."
title: "China K-12 Subject Knowledge Graph (cn-k12-dxyc2286)"
abstract: >-
  An open knowledge graph covering 18 school subjects from primary to senior high
  school in mainland China: 12,269 knowledge nodes across 19 subjects and 55 subject tracks,
  13,686 prerequisite edges (13,194 hard / 492 soft), 80,539 node-level diagnostic
  items, and 4,375 curriculum-standard entries (12,034 knowledge nodes carry a
  quoted standard excerpt plus a confidence score). Each node ships an observable mastery criterion and
  diagnostic items, so the graph can drive prerequisite diagnosis and learning
  path recommendation directly.
